course: dictionary
lesson: 6419
title: Mutation: a change in genes or in words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mutation is a change. In biology, it is a change in the genes (DNA) of a living thing, and it can give that living thing a new feature. «Mutations are the raw material of evolution» means that these changes are what evolution works with.
explain: Most mutations make no difference, some are harmful and a few are helpful. Context shows you this: «Changes in DNA are called mutations; they happen when cells copy DNA with small mistakes, and most do nothing, some are harmful and a few are useful.» The mistake in copying is the clue to what a mutation is, and the words most, some and a few tell you how common each kind is.
explain: A mutation can also be any change from one shape or kind into another. In Welsh and Irish, it means a change to the first sound of a word. Ffion in Cardiff says «cath» for cat but «fy nghath» for «my cat», so the first sound changes after a small word. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A mutation is a change in the genes (DNA) of a living thing.
fact: Mutations happen when cells copy DNA with small mistakes.
fact: Most mutations make no difference; some are harmful and a few are helpful.
fact: In comics and films, mutations that give superheroes strange powers are fiction, not real science.
fact: In the news, virus mutations can create new variants.
exercise: «Changes in DNA are called mutations.» In this sentence, what is a mutation? | A long journey by boat | *A change in the genes (DNA) of a living thing | A kind of pet | A type of weather
exercise: In Welsh, «cath» becomes «fy nghath» for «my cat». What changes in a mutation like this? | The colour of the page | *The first sound of the word | The number of words in the sentence | The last full stop
exercise: «Most mutations make no difference.» What does most mean here? | Exactly one | *More than half | None at all | A small number
test: Which statement is true? | Mutations only happen in comics | Mutations are only ever harmful | Mutations are a kind of food | *Some mutations are helpful, and most make no difference
test: Is a mutation that gives a hero superpowers real science? | Yes, it is in every science lesson | Yes, but only in Wales | *No, it is fiction | Yes, every mutation gives powers
exam: Which sentence uses mutation to mean a change from one shape or kind into another? | *The toy's mutation from a car into a robot amazed the children | The mutation was a bright red coat for winter | A mutation is a kind of dinner eaten in the afternoon | The mutation of the lesson was a long walk home
